===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|sol||fifth degree or note of Guido of Arezzo’s hexachordal scales}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|pos=''n.''(2)|noformat=1|id=MED41379}}</ref> the first {{glossary|syllable}} of {{der|en|la|solve||to remove; to get rid of}}, the first word of the fifth line, third verse (“Solve polluti, labii reatum”, that is, “Clean the guilt from our stained lips”) of the famed medieval hymn ''[[w:Ut queant laxis|Ut queant laxis]]'', which [[solfège]] was based on because its lines started on each note of the scale successively.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=''n.''{{sup|2}}|noformat=1|id=184023|date=December 2020|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=sol{{sup|1}}|pos=n}}</ref>

