* {{a|GA}} {{enPR|sōl}}, {{IPA|en|/sɔl/|/sɑl/|/soʊl/}}
* {{homophones|en|soul|sole}} {{q|Canada|US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒl|əʊl|s=1}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{senseid|en|solfege}}{{lb|en|music}}
## In a [[movable#Adjective|movable]]-[[do]] or [[tonic#Adjective|tonic]] [[sol-fa]] [[system]]: the [[fifth]] [[step#Noun|step]] in a [[scale#Noun|scale]], [[precede]]d by [[fa]] and [[follow]]ed by [[la]].
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|act=III|scene=i|page=218|column=2|passage=''D '''ſol''' re'', one [[clef|Cliffe]], two notes haue I, / ''Ela mi'', ſhow pitty or I die.}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet Q1-2|act=IV|scene=v|page=69|passage=''Ser''[''vant'', ''i.e.'', Peter]. Alack alack what ſhal I doe, come Fidlers play me ſome mery dumpe. / ''I.'' [''First musician'']. A ſir, this is no time to play. / {{...}} / ''Ser.'' Then will I giue it you, and ſoundly to. / ''I.'' What will you giue vs? / ''Ser.'' The fidler, Ile re you, Ile fa you, Ile '''ſol''' you. / ''I.'' If you re vs and fa vs, we will note you.|footer=A {{glossary|nonce}} use as a verb.|brackets=on}}
## In a [[fixed#Adjective|fixed]]-do system: the [[musical#Adjective|musical]] [[note#Noun|note]] [[G]].

